---
description: BoI Wiki Local workspace rules
alwaysApply: true
---

This workspace is a Local Private BoI folder.

- Start from `data/boi/index.md` and folder `index.md` files.
- Do not scan everything first unless broad cleanup/search is requested.
- Before writing personal BoI documents, confirm a numeric 7-digit employee ID from `BOI_LOCAL_EMPLOYEE_ID` or the user.
- Save personal BoI documents under `data/boi/private/{employee_id}/`.
- Save diagrams, event/workflow-definition drafts, context packs, pre-execution simulations, and Langflow plans in their matching folders under `data/boi/private/{employee_id}/`.
- One-off or repeated personal work can start as a Local Private work BoI without forcing an SOP.
- Save dictionary terms under `data/boi/private/{employee_id}/dictionary/`.
- For bulk dictionary candidates, record `keep`, `replace_with_canonical`, `split_into_terms`, `alias_to_existing`, `exclude`, or `needs_parent_curation` in local candidate/override/manifest or promotion drafts instead of changing code per term.
- Required metadata includes `employee_id`, `local_owner_ref`, `visibility: local-private`, `local_only: true`, `promotion_status`, lifecycle fields, and `source_refs`.
- Update `index.md` and `log.md` after changes.
- Run self-check before completion. Use `check.sh` or `check.ps1` if available.
- MCP is optional. If not available, use local files and user-provided sources. Do not require a local MCP server; the official optional MCP is shared BoI Wiki MCP.
- If MCP is available, use `dictionary_resolve` for terms before interpreting acronyms, `ontology_search` for broad knowledge lookup, `workflow_definitions_search` and `workflow_definition_deduplicate` before proposing new shared workflow definitions, `boi_agent_chat` for page-aware questions, `agent_inbox` for assigned tasks, and `boi_search` only for document-only search.
- Never send Local Private originals remotely without explicit user confirmation.
- For Team/Public sharing, create a sanitized promotion draft, run preflight, show preview, then submit remote sync validation/publish only after explicit confirmation. Remote validation, commit, publish, and HOTL status are handled by BoI Wiki; do not ask the user to run Git commands.
